      "writtenOn": "2022-12-07T17:04:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have some questions for your consideration: Is it intentional that we pass in a *copy* of a Dawn queue into the queue manager? I do see that you call std::move on the queue in the constructor, but it\u0027s not immediately apparent that both classes can\u0027t have their own copies. I believe we want the backend context and the queue manager to point towards one synchronous queue object, so it might be more explicit to pass around the queue by reference (either a smart pointer, an actual reference, etc.). \n\nBasically, between the queue manager and the backend context, who *owns* the queue and who should be able to change it? The answer to that question can guide what we do next.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "87191acd5863ab0dd9ceef3ce0cf89a82d76216c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7dbc3714_7ca1ebfb",
